<Doc title="Terms" description="The rules for playing Who's Cooked? and buying Cooked+.">
  <p><strong>Draft, pending legal review.</strong> Last updated 7 November 2026.</p>

  <h2>The game</h2>
  <p>
    Who's Cooked? is a game for fun. It isn't a medical, psychological, or relationship test, and your score says
    nothing about you beyond how this game went. Practice gets you better at this game. We don't claim it improves
    attention or anything else in daily life.
  </p>

  <h2>Cooked+ and Chaos Crew</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Cooked+ and Chaos Crew are one-time digital purchases. They don't renew, and there's no subscription, no in-game currency, and no random rewards.</li>
    <li>Cooked+ adds the Daily archive, two characters, full stats, and a frame on share cards. Chaos Crew adds three characters. Neither changes how the game is scored.</li>
    <li>The price is shown before checkout, including tax where required.</li>
    <li>Players under 13 can't buy them. Players aged 13 to 17 need a parent or guardian to complete checkout.</li>
    <li>Access is tied to the device you bought on. You can restore it on another device with the details from your receipt.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Refunds</h2>
  <p>
    If something went wrong, contact <a href="mailto:support@whoscooked.com">support@whoscooked.com</a> within 14 days
    and we'll make it right. Purchases are handled by our payment provider (the merchant of record), whose refund terms
    also apply. Refunded purchases lose access.
  </p>

  <h2>Fair play and leaderboards</h2>
  <p>Don't use bots or scripts to play. Scores from automated play may be removed. Leaderboards are for players 13 and up and use generated handles only.</p>
</Doc>
